# ── LeadFinder daily scout ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# With config.CITIES and config.CATEGORIES now covering 9 cities and 50+
# categories, a full run is city × category searches (400-500+), each
# with a 2-5 second throttling delay per TRAI compliance (T2.1).
#
# Schedule this at least 60-90 minutes before you'd actually want fresh
# leads ready — not the quick few-minute run a single-city/single-category
# example might imply.
#
# Example: for leads ready by 09:00, schedule at 07:30 or earlier.
# Daily at 7:30 AM:
#   30 7 * * * cd /path/to/LeadFinder && .venv/bin/python scripts/run_daily.py
#
# ── Guard against double-scout ─────────────────────────────────────────
# If the dashboard's background trigger (scripts/auto_scout_runner.py)
# already ran today's scout (e.g. because you opened the dashboard before
# this cron time), run_daily.py will detect get_last_scout_date() == today
# and skip its own pipeline automatically.
